CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ path from a std::string is not empty: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [fs.path.construct]/5: path(const Source &) with a std::string source
stores the string, so the path is not empty.  Fixed (round 163w): the
constructor called the generic __detail::__effective_range(const _Source &)
instead of the basic_string overload, because candidates were ranked by
their number of template arguments before partial ordering
(cpp11_partial_ordering_ignores_template_argument_count); _S_convert then
saw `int'.  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
